  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) at 0.653 acc. The key remaining question is whether adding the image modality to this best RNA setup can push accuracy higher. Image alone is weak (resnet50: 0.208), but it may carry complementary spatial/morphological information. Config_032 tests multimodal fusion (concat) with the exact best RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) plus resnet50, isolating the effect of adding image. This is the highest-value experiment because: (1) it directly tests whether multimodal can beat the 0.653 ceiling, (2) if it helps, the remaining 2 experiments can explore ViT-L or weighted fusion to push further, and (3) if it doesn't help, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can spend remaining budget on minor RNA-side refinements. Concat is chosen over weighted as the simpler, more standard baseline fusion to first establish whether image adds any signal."
}

